  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124471,
      "id": "ea1e5a55-a957-52cd-b693-0e48770672a6",
      "title": "Computing the Rate of Change of a Multivariable Function at a Point Using the Chain Rule"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bca961ad-ef95-5011-80d3-fc937feaf8af",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=- x^{2} - y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)=⟨3 t - 2,3 t⟩$ at the point $t=-1.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- x^{2} - y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- x^{2} - y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 2 x,- 2 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=3 t - 2$, $y=3 t$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =⟨- 2 \\left(3 t - 2\\right),- 2 \\cdot 3 t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 4,- 6 t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t - 2),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 4,- 6 t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(- 6 t + 4\\right)\\cdot \\left(3\\right)+\\left(- 6 t\\right)\\cdot \\left(3\\right) \\\\  & =- 36 t + 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ at $t=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(-1))] & =- 36 (-1) + 12 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
